It works. Here's the full program:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Text.Json;

public record Person(string name, int age);

class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        var person = new Person("Alice", 30);
        var options = new JsonSerializerOptions
        {
            PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase
        };
        string json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(person, options);
        Console.WriteLine(json);
    }
}
```

**Output:** `{"Name":"Alice","Age":30}`

.NET 11 adds `JsonNamingPolicy.PascalCase` as a built-in policy (joining `CamelCase`, `SnakeCaseLower`, etc. from earlier releases). It converts your lowercase record parameter names (`name`, `age`) to PascalCase (`Name`, `Age`) in the serialized JSON — no custom naming policy needed.
